  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Chikuzen biwa, a Japanese narrative biwa song, took shape in Hakata in the Meiji era, when the blind-priest biwa of the Chikuzen region was reworked with the melodic style of shamisen music, and it spread nationally through the Tachibana and Asahi schools as a genre performed largely by women. Its instrument is a lighter four- or five-string biwa played with a smaller plectrum than the Satsuma biwa.",
